<title>ITALY: Gemina shareholders aprove spinoff plan.</title>
<headline>Gemina shareholders aprove spinoff plan.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Gemina approved by a wide majority at a meeting on Thursday a plan to spin off the holding company's industrial assets into a new holding company called Holding Partecipazioni Industriali (HPI).</p>
<p>HPI will have net equity of 2.075 trillion lire while Gemina, which will be left holding a clutch of financial assets, will have net equity of 248 billion lire.</p>
<p>Shareholders were also due to vote on a plan to seek a bourse listing for HPI.</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom 392-66102321</p>
